    "raw_text": "Security & Safe Usage FAQ\nDomain: Basic account and application security practices.\nDataset purpose: This document is a sample knowledge-base source for a Multimodal\nRetrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) FAQ system.\nThe visual above is intentionally embedded so the data-extraction module can detect and extract images from the PDF.\nQ1. How can I identify a suspicious login page?\nCheck the website address carefully and verify that the connection uses HTTPS. Be cautious of unexpected\nmessages asking for passwords or one-time codes.\nQ2. Should I share my OTP with support staff?\nDo not share passwords or one-time authentication codes with another person. Use the official support\nprocess if you need help.\nQ3. What should I do after clicking a suspicious link?\nDo not enter credentials on the suspicious page. Close it and follow your organization's or service provider's\nsecurity-reporting procedure.\nQ4. Why should I use a strong password?\nA strong password makes unauthorized access more difficult. Use a unique password for important\naccounts and follow the service's password requirements.\nSource type: Synthetic sample FAQ document | Suitable for local development and extraction testing.",
